### REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client file. Order-service on :8080, review-service on :8083.

### Menu
GET http://localhost:8080/dishes

### One dish
GET http://localhost:8080/dishes/1

### Dish not found -> 404
GET http://localhost:8080/dishes/999

### Place an order -> 201 (409 sold out, 404 unknown dish, 400 invalid quantity, 502 payment failed)
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dishId": 2, "quantity": 2}

### Invalid quantity -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dishId": 2, "quantity": 0}

### Unknown dish -> 404
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"dishId": 999, "quantity": 1}

### Get an order
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/1

### Review -> 202 Accepted with no body
POST http://localhost:8080/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"dishId": 1, "rating": 5, "comment": "Great"}

### Invalid rating -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"dishId": 1, "rating": 9, "comment": "Too much"}

### Ranking (read from the database by review-service)
GET http://localhost:8083/reviews/ranking

### Assistant: on topic
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Tem prato vegetariano até R$ 40?"}

### Assistant: off topic (must be politely refused)
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Quem ganhou a Copa de 2002?"}

### Eureka registry (JSON)
GET http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps
Accept: application/json
